**.vscode/
**.idea/

**.DS_Store

**target/
**Cargo.lock
# ...except the downstream fixture's, and the exception is load-bearing. `ci/downstream.sh` passes
# `--locked` to every leg so the gate is hermetic: it answers "does smear's feature gate what it
# advertises", which has nothing to do with which patch of a dependency is current, and an unpinned
# resolve would make a red read "upstream released something". `--locked` with no committed lock is
# a hard cargo error, so ignoring this file would leave the gate unable to run at all.
!ci/downstream/Cargo.lock

**wip

# Local design docs / plans / investigation reports (never committed; see
# team convention — the issue tracker is for defects and measurable
# optimisations, docs/ is for everything else).
#
# Root-anchored on purpose: a leading "/" with no "**" prefix, unlike the
# patterns above. This repo's other entries are meant to match at any depth
# (a build `target/` or stray `.DS_Store` can appear under any crate), but
# this one must not — it should catch only the top-level docs/ tree, not a
# nested `*/docs/` directory some crate might add later (e.g. doc assets
# under `smear-lexer/docs/`). Verified with `git check-ignore -v`: bare
# `docs/` and `**docs/` both match at *any* depth (git only anchors a
# pattern when it has a leading or middle slash — a trailing slash alone
# does not anchor it), so neither achieves "root tree only". `/docs/` does.
/docs/